SURFACE (web-source parity; no stubs / skeletons / placeholders)
- Chrome: shared ToolCard (cyan accent, Segoe Fluent "Library" glyph = the house Segoe analogue of the
  web Lucide BookOpen, title 'Tesla Api Ref', description 'Tesla Api Ref Desc').
- Body: a search field (TsInput, leading glyph, 'Search Endpoints' hint) over a paged 3-column reference
  table built from the static TESLA_ENDPOINTS catalog (11 rows):
    * Method        -> TsBadge, info(GET)/warning(write verbs)   [web variant={method==='GET'?'info':'warning'}]
    * Path          -> monospace accent text + TsCopyButton       [web <code> + <CopyButton text={path}/>]
    * Endpoint Desc -> secondary text
  Pagination via TsPagination (web DataTable `pagination`, page size 25).
- States (every state renders, never a blank box): Populated, and Empty -> TsEmptyState with a friendly
  title + message when the search filter matches nothing. The tool performs NO I/O over a static constant
  (its only web hook is useTranslation), so there is no loading/error/stale/offline branch to reproduce —
  honest parity, identical to the sibling Base64Tool's documented reasoning.
- Shared components only: ToolCard, TsInput, TsBadge, TsCopyButton, TsPagination, TsEmptyState,
  DisplayTokens. No direct library imports, no raw HTML, tokenized (no ad-hoc hex / inline styles).
- i18n: every string resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade. Keys mirror the web t() call sites
  exactly: 'Tesla Api Ref', 'Tesla Api Ref Desc', 'Search Endpoints', 'Method', 'Path', 'Endpoint Desc',
  'common.copyButton.copy', 'common.copyButton.copied', pagination.first/previous/next/last,
  a11y.pagination, plus the native empty-state keys devtools.teslaApiRef.emptyTitle/emptyMessage.
  Catalog parity: the keys the WEB en.json defines for this surface (Method, Path, common.copyButton.*)
  are present in the Windows catalog (apps/windows/Strings/*/Resources.resw); the four descriptive keys
  ('Tesla Api Ref', 'Tesla Api Ref Desc', 'Search Endpoints', 'Endpoint Desc') are ABSENT in BOTH the web
  en.json AND the Windows catalog, so the facade fallback renders text identical to the web (i18next
  missing-key -> key string). No catalog edit is required; adding those keys would diverge from the source.
- Accessibility: Narrator names on the search field, the table region, every per-row copy button (each
  names the path it copies), and the pager; decorative glyphs marked AccessibilityView.Raw.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): emits `view.opened slug=TeslaApiRefTool`, PII-safe (never the search query or rows).

DATA ADAPTER + STATE HOLDER (UI-free, unit-tested)
- TeslaApiEndpoint (record) + TeslaApiEndpointCatalog (11 endpoints, verbatim TESLA_ENDPOINTS).
- TeslaApiRefFilter.Apply — pure port of the web useMemo filter: empty/whitespace query -> full catalog
  (web `if (!search.trim()) return TESLA_ENDPOINTS`); otherwise the (un-trimmed) query is matched
  case-insensitively against method/path/desc.
- TeslaApiRefToolViewModel — search -> filtered/paged projection + state + localized labels + a11y names;
  resets to page one on search change (web DataTable behaviour).

